Variables

A variable is a named container used to store data that can be used and changed in a program.

1. let

Used when the variable's value may change.

let age = 20;
age = 21;
2. const

Used when the variable's value should not be reassigned.

const pi = 3.14;
3. var

Older way of declaring variables. It is generally avoided in modern JavaScript because let and const are safer and clearer.

var name = "Hamza";
name = "Ali";
Declaration

Declaration means creating a variable without giving it a value.

let age;
Initialization

Initialization means giving a variable its first value.

let age = 20;
Declaration + Initialization Together
let age = 20;

Here, let age is the declaration, and = 20 is the initialization.
